WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:03.550
Do you care about politics?

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:09.309
Or maybe I should rather ask, do you care
about politics in your favourite show or series?

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:14.300
Regardless, whether you answer this question
with yes or no, you may not be aware of HOW

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.480
big a deal thoughtful political writing can
be in storytelling.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.480
Because the truth is: Deep down, we all DO
care how things are being run in the world

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.039
our heroes live in, and also by whom.

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:31.769
This is ESPECIALLY obvious for stories where
the political system is unfair or straight

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:32.989
out evil.

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:37.399
And political structures can give a story
world a level of colour and realism, that

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:40.059
makes it INCREDIBLY easy to engage with.

00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:45.980
But, when I talk about politics, I in no way
mean focusing purely on political manoeuvring.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.859
After all, most of us don’t want every story
to be a House of Cards.

00:00:49.859 --> 00:00:55.510
Much rather, good political writing usually
is SUBTLE and only throws us small bits and

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.089
pieces of the overarching structure of the
society our heroes live in.

00:01:00.089 --> 00:01:04.940
While modern television has discovered the
value of political intrigue and action, Shounen

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:10.080
manga might not exactly be the FIRST genre
that comes to your mind in this context.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.829
And yet, one of the reasons One Piece has
managed to become as POPULAR as it is today,

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:19.610
is the political aspect Oda has increasingly
integrated into his story.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:25.159
In fact, one character in particular has enriched
One Piece in a NUMBER of ways, that might

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:27.759
not be obvious at first glance.

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:32.759
Because Vivi is a wonderful example of political
writing done right.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:37.820
With her introduction to the story, Oda also
introduces a proper political system for the

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.189
first time, that made the overall story more
entertaining, and successfully distinguished

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:45.890
it from other Shounen mangas competing with
it over the years.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.359
Vivi´s character arc shows her growing into
a great political leader, and gives us an

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:53.479
idea of Oda´s own political values.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:58.139
Not only does Vivi trigger important character
and story development by teaching Luffy to

00:01:58.139 --> 00:02:02.909
become a better leader himself, but she also
enhances our perception of the straw hat crew

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:08.600
in GENREAL by clearly contrasting what makes
them so unique in the One Piece universe.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:13.540
And I think that this power of political writing,
especially in the sub-genre of Shounen manga,

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.090
is worth taking a closer look at.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:20.319
Because bedding their adventure in a sense
of realism, allows our heroes to break out

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:25.099
of these every-day conventions we are familiar
with, and thus in turn help US escape from

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:30.040
our everyday lives.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.989
What makes Vivi so different from any other
character that we have met in the story up

00:02:33.989 --> 00:02:39.519
to this point, is that her character arc is
not the story of a pirate, but the story of

00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:40.849
a leader.

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:45.680
After the introductory arcs of the East Blue,
meeting Vivi is the beginning of the first

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.400
REAL saga in the straw hats’ adventure,
spanning over multiple different arcs.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.680
Getting to know the princess of Alabasta and
witnessing her struggle to free her country

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.439
from the grasp of one of the seven Warlords
of the sea, introduces a conflict on a much

00:02:59.439 --> 00:03:03.700
larger scale than anything we had gotten up
to this point.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.530
Being a compassionate and brave young woman,
that cares deeply for her people, it quickly

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:12.810
becomes clear that her task is not to get
physically stronger in order to take down

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:17.700
her political opponent crocodile, but rather
to become a better politician herself.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:23.470
To do so, right from the get-go, Oda already
equipped her character with a number of traits

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:28.590
that show us her true potential as a leader
very early on in the story.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:32.969
Even as a kid, Vivi already shows a notch
for politics and diplomacy.

00:03:32.969 --> 00:03:37.580
When slapped by an angry Wapol, she keeps
her cool not to cause a major international

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.870
incident for her father and country.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:44.710
She also befriends a group of common kids,
including the young Koza, who later would

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:48.270
lead the rebellion in the civil war staged
by Crocodile.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:52.939
And in general, far from being authoritative
and tempered, Vivi fulfils the trope of the

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:57.950
kind and adventurous princess, that is brave
and determined to take action for her country’s

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:58.950
sake.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:03.340
Thus, she doesn’t hesitate to infiltrate
Corcodile´s Baroque-Work agency at the age

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.519
of only fourteen and works her way up the
ladder over a two-year period, in which she

00:04:08.519 --> 00:04:10.400
even learns how to fight.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.810
Further, she is also CLEARLY able to deal
with pain, be it physical from being shot

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:19.640
in the shoulder, or psychological from loosing
Igaram.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:24.760
So, when she meets Luffy, who very quickly
comes to acknowledge her determination, she

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.730
already shows enormous promise to become a
great leader in the future.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:34.500
However, Crocodile manipulating her country
into famine, and ultimately civil war, proves

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:39.860
to be too much for her to handle and she suffers
deeply under her people’s hardship.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:44.100
Falsely believing that she has to carry her
country’s burden all on her own, it takes

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.140
a quite emotional brawl with Luffy, to show
her that she needs to believe in her friends

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.640
and let them share in on her load.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:56.290
Still, in spite of Luffy´s speech she once
again tries to end the bloody battle between

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.440
the royal army and the rebells all by herself.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:04.140
Not only does she fail to be heard, she also
fails to stop the bomb planted by Crocodile

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.040
in the middle of the city.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.830
This is the low-point of her character arc.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:14.510
However, Luffy defeating Crocodile and finally
returning the rain, as well as Pell sacrificing

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:19.420
himself by carrying the bomb away from the
city, finally help Vivi in overcoming her

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.290
biggest weakness as a leader.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:27.670
Thus, in her coming of age speech, we finally
see a future Queen that has grown significantly

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:33.020
through her shared adventures with the straw
hats.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:37.990
In contrast to the power-focused pirate battles
we had seen up to this point, Vivi introduces

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:42.630
a political level to the story that up to
this day helps distinguishing it from other

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:43.830
Shounen.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:48.620
Alabasta and the Baroque work saga are the
first real taste of political intrigue and

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:54.170
conflict in One Piece, way before arcs like
Enis Lobby or Dressrosa, that are even more

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.710
centred around political themes.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:02.550
With crocodile, for the first time we encounter
an antagonist that cannot simply be beaten

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:07.940
by pure strength alone, but rather has to
be approached in multiple steps over multiple

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:11.520
arcs, requiring the skills of the ENTIRE crew.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:16.520
This brings an entirely new level of complexity
and tension into the story, that not only

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:21.380
make the story less predictable, but also
requires more thoughtful and creative action

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.720
from our heroes.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:27.970
Similarly, the political level of Alabasta,
also enlarges the entire story world we had

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.330
known up to this point.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:33.910
For the first time, it becomes clear that
the One Piece world does not only consist

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.860
of small islands with quiet villages, as we
exclusively have seen in the East Blue.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:44.020
Much rather, we learn that many islands consist
of entire kingdoms, with their own political

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:48.970
systems that have existed for hundreds, if
not thousands of years.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:53.690
This insight broadens our view on the world
immensely and prepares us for the overarching

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:55.480
conflict with the world government.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:07:01.800
Thus Vivi´s character enables important story
development over all.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.150
But I think it goes even further than this.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:10.570
Because she also triggers important character
development for the entire crew, and especially

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.910
so for Luffy.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:16.960
See, while Luffy teaches Vivi about the importance
of trusting in your friends and sharing a

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:22.150
burden, Vivi in turn teaches Luffy a CRUCIAL
lesson about leadership.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:26.700
After leaving Little Garden, Vivi convinces
the crew to make a detour for the severely

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:29.950
ill Nami and find a doctor on Drum Island.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:34.650
Upon arriving at a small village on the islands
shore, the villagers, lead by the future king

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:38.130
Dalton, surround the ship and beckon the crew
to turn around.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:43.470
In the course of this tense situation, Vivi
is shot in the shoulder.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:49.470
Seeing his friend being hurt, Luffy, as he
always does, starts charging at the villagers.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:54.700
However Vivi stops him in the last moment
and bows down to the villagers in apology.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.680
She calls out Luffy for his rash reaction
that might have cost Nami´s life.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:04.370
In this moment, Luffy makes a graspable leap
in his character development.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:09.360
He bows down himself and asks for help to
save his navigator.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:14.730
The IMPORTANT lesson, that Vivi taught Luffy
here, is that some situations cannot simply

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.380
be solved through fighting alone.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:22.220
Some situations call for diplomacy, strategy
or even humility.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:26.510
This ultimately helps Luffy to become a better
leader himself.

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:30.240
And we can actually see his growth from this
scene in later arcs.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:35.219
On Sabaody for instance, Luffy actually orders
his crew to flee, realising that fighting

00:08:35.219 --> 00:08:38.360
against an admiral is futile at this point.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:43.659
And on Jaya, he and Zoro do not fight back
against Bellamy´s men, just like Shanks did

00:08:43.659 --> 00:08:46.910
not fight back against the bandits back when
Luffy was a kid.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:52.569
Thus, Luffy has gotten a step closer to Shanks’
ideal of a great pirate, all through learning

00:08:52.569 --> 00:08:58.480
from Vivi´s words.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.230
And aside from her personal influence on Luffy
and the others, her character benefits US,

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.230
the readers, even more.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:10.829
Vivi is a character that is caught in the
gruesome normality of the One Piece world.

00:09:10.829 --> 00:09:14.829
No matter how hard she tries to take things
into her own hands and change them with all

00:09:14.829 --> 00:09:19.410
her might, she doesn’t seem able to escape
the grasps of the powerful forces at work

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.410
in her country.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:25.420
And while it is easy to confuse her normality,
helplessness and frustration as something

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:29.980
of little importance when looking at it through
the lens of typical Shounen stories, what

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:34.980
Vivi´s character ACTUALLY does for us, is
contrasting how unique and special Luffy and

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.160
his crew are in this unforgiving system.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:42.870
How they are actually physically and mentally
strong enough to take on these major forces

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:45.220
at work in the One Piece world.

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:49.610
This is the TRUE secret of the success Vivi
has brought to Oda´s story.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:54.950
She allows us to widen our focus and shows
us that Luffy, Zoro and Co. are indeed NOT

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.449
normal.

00:09:56.449 --> 00:10:01.079
This makes their adventure just the more exciting,
as we now know just HOW unique they actually

00:10:01.079 --> 00:10:06.029
are inside this complex political web of powerful
and influential people.

00:10:06.029 --> 00:10:10.879
Being able to carry out this fundamental change
in his approach to story-telling in such a

00:10:10.879 --> 00:10:15.370
seamless way, is part of the genius of Oda´s
writing.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:19.560
Subtly integrating such conceptual layers
beneath the main plot line, and thus being

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:24.620
able to share a richer and more vivid world
with us readers, is what I find truly thrilling

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:27.139
about One Piece as a piece of literature.

00:10:27.139 --> 00:10:32.310
After all, writing a character like Vivi takes
not only a lot of creativity and skill, but

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:37.720
also a signifiant portion of bravery, in a
genre that otherwise has been heavily dominated

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.110
by ever-repeating power-struggles.

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:45.720
However, far from making One Piece LESS exciting
or intense, political characters like Vivi

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:51.249
actually ENHANCE and CONTRAST the protagonists,
and help bring out the best in them.

00:10:51.249 --> 00:10:55.410
So, in the end, you may think that you don’t
care about politics in your favourite story

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:59.209
- until you find out that you actually do.

00:10:59.209 --> 00:11:07.560
Maybe just not quite in the way, that you
expected to.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.100
Hey everyone, thank you so much for watching.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:13.100
What are your thoughts on Vivi and her role
in the story?

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.589
And what character would you like to see me
discuss next?

00:11:15.589 --> 00:11:18.550
Share your thoughts with me in the comments
below.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:22.430
